vectorwake (criccomini, push to main): Subspace-inspired space MMO. Docs in docs/, deterministic C sim core in sim/, playable wasm client in client-web/. Own art and ships; server-authoritative; AI bots via inputs only.                                                                    
vectorwake through M5.5: deterministic core, server-authoritative arena with Elo attribution, duels and warzone, Defold client playing offline and networked; controls arrows+Space+Shift.                                                                                                     
The client grew multiplayer, call signs, typed map tiles and map files -- and a silent build failure shipped three stale artifacts, now guarded by an on-screen commit stamp.                                                                                                                  
Check build exit codes; profile the browser not native. Zones own their rules, sent over the wire. Weapons are one table model with a tech tree of levels, add-ons and charges. Bounty is derived from what you hold; points are the victim's bounty.                                          
Matched the original's numbers (prize weights, multifire cost, charges and add-ons universal, its nine per-ship settings), opened the map to all 1024 tiles, halved snapshots, sped up sim_step, and rebuilt the mobile HUD around a d-pad.                                                    
Mobile keeps the plain pointing stick and has no reverse; five schemes lost to it. Duels are out for now. Hosting is Vultr, cost is egress not compute. ASSS ships no per-ship balance and no arena cap, so the roster is ours. Repel is hostile only.                                         
The fleet was designed, tuned to the original's numbers, and shipped: docs closed their questions, the roster went authentic, and the game ended up live and hardened on a Vultr box behind Caddy.                                                                                             
vectorwake went live and every real bug was found by playing it, never by a health check: dead combat, frozen bots, unfindable greens and flags, a stale bundle. The build moved to CI along the way.                                                                                          
2026-08-03 The live fleet's quiet failures found and fixed: a stale bundle, two open sockets, an unreachable ladder, a roster sent once, a narrow Docker context, no spawn kit, bots stuck on walls, input timing. Offline mode removed. Decision 29 designed.                                 
